WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.912
Why this matters to everyone
who works in an agency.

2
00:00:02.912 --> 00:00:06.517
In many agencies Active
Directory feeds the phone book,

3
00:00:06.517 --> 00:00:09.337
and nothing feeds Active
Directory from HR.

4
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:12.471
Titles, offices, phone
numbers and managers stay

5
00:00:12.471 --> 00:00:15.526
wrong until someone
notices and files a ticket.

6
00:00:15.526 --> 00:00:20.426
And every time someone changes management,
their organization, their manager

7
00:00:20.426 --> 00:00:25.100
and their access to tools have to be
updated by hand, after the fact, by ticket.

8
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.912
HR already knows all of it.

9
00:00:26.912 --> 00:00:31.914
With HR-driven IT, the personnel action
that records the reassignment updates the

10
00:00:31.914 --> 00:00:36.621
organization and manager in Entra ID and
Active Directory, and the phone book,

11
00:00:36.621 --> 00:00:41.108
the approval chain and tool access
follow from the authoritative source —

12
00:00:41.108 --> 00:00:45.600
instead of each person, and the help
desk, keeping them current by hand.
